# [[particular|Particular]], [[specific]].
#: {{ux|en|No more than three people can be in that space at a '''given''' time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1791|author=[[w:Thomas Paine|Thomas Paine]]|title=Rights of Man|chapter=Miscellaneous Chapter|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Rights_of_Man
|text=If, therefore, the amount of the annual importation into Europe can be known, and the relative proportion of the foreign commerce of the several nations by which it can be distributed can be ascertained, they give a rule sufficiently true, to ascertain the quantity of money which ought to be found in any nation, at any '''given''' time.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1907|author=[[w:Pope Pius X|Pope Pius X]]|title=Pascendi Dominici Gregis|chapter=Analysis of Modernist Teaching|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Pascendi
|text=Thus we have a double Christ: a real Christ, and a Christ, the one of faith, who never really existed; a Christ who has lived at a '''given''' time and in a '''given''' place, and a Christ who has never lived outside the pious meditations of the believer - the Christ, for instance, whom we find in the Gospel of St. John, which is pure contemplation from beginning to end.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1976|author=[[w:Carlo M. Cipolla|Carlo M. Cipolla]]|title=The Basic Laws of Human Stupidity|chapter=Frequency distribution|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Basic_Laws_of_Human_Stupidity
|text=Most people do not act consistently. Under certain circumstances a '''given''' person acts intelligently and under different circumstances the same person will act helplessly.}}
# [[assumed|Assumed]] as fact or hypothesis.
#: {{ux|en|'''Given''' that we will get the resources, what do we want to achieve?}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1874|author=[[w:Lewis Carroll|Lewis Carroll]]|title=The Dynamics of a Parti-cle|chapter=Chapter II: Dynamics of a Particle|page=19|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/The_Dynamics_of_a_Parti-cle
|text=''Example.'' '''Given''' a Derby Prophet, who has sent 3 different winners to 3 different betting-men, and '''given''' that none of the three horses are placed. Find the total Loss incurred by the three men (α) in money, (β) in temper.}}
#* {{quote-hansard|en|date=1994-02-24|speaker=Eleni Bakopanos|house=House of Commons of Canada|url=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Debates_of_the_House_of_Commons_of_Canada_(Hansard)_-_Thursday,_February_24,_1994_-_Government_Orders
|text='''Given''' the narrow vision of the opposition, and '''given''' that it keeps saying the same things, I would like to know why these separatists&mdash;after all this is their real name&mdash;insist on continually misleading Quebecers and not telling them the truth.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2017-11-06|author=Fiann M. Smithwick;Robert Nicholls;Innes C. Cuthill;Jakob Vinther|article=Countershading and Stripes in the Theropod Dinosaur ''Sinosauropteryx'' Reveal Heterogeneous Habitats in the Early Cretaceous Jehol Biota|journal=Elsevier|volume=27|issue=21|section=Discussion|page=3|articleurl=https://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Countershading_and_Stripes_in_the_Theropod_Dinosaur_Sinosauropteryx_Reveal_Heterogeneous_Habitats_in_the_Early_Cretaceous_Jehol_Biota
|text=Pigmented bands that run directly across the orbital region may also help to mask the presence of the eyes as a form of camouflage against both predators and potential prey [20, 21]. Eye stripes are common in modern birds, which most often also have dark eyes, making them likely harder for visual predators or prey to detect, and '''given''' that eyes elicit responses from both in many situations, it is a plausible hypothesis [13].}}
# {{senseid|en|prone, disposed}}{{lb|en|with ''to''}} [[prone|Prone]], [[disposed]].
#: {{ux|en|He was '''given''' to taking a couple of glasses of port at his club.}}

